# eBike project — custom Kconfig options.

mainmenu "eBike firmware"

# === Cellular connectivity ===================================================

config EBIKE_APN
	string "SIM APN (empty = APN supplied by the network)"
	default ""
	help
	  Access Point Name forced on the default PDP context (CID 0). Leave
	  empty to let the network provide it, which is what most LTE-M IoT
	  SIMs expect. Requires CONFIG_LTE_LC_PDN_MODULE=y.

config EBIKE_PDN_IPV4_ONLY
	bool "Request an IPv4-only default PDP context"
	default n
	help
	  Diagnostic fallback: ask for IPv4 instead of IPv4v6, as some visited
	  networks reject the IPV4V6 type. No effect when EBIKE_APN is empty.

# === Shared runtime defaults (carried on CH_CONFIG) ==========================

config EBIKE_PUBLISH_RIDING_S
	int "Publish interval while riding (seconds)"
	default 60
	range 10 3600
	help
	  Interval between MQTT publications when the bike is moving. Below
	  60 s the LTE link stays in RRC connected almost permanently and
	  starves the GNSS receiver.

config EBIKE_MOTION_THRESHOLD_MG
	int "IMU motion detection threshold (milli-g)"
	default 150
	range 10 2000
	help
	  Norm of the acceleration delta between two IMU polls above which
	  movement is reported. Using the delta cancels gravity, so the test is
	  insensitive to how the bike is oriented. 150 mg ignores sensor noise
	  (~10-20 mg) while still catching someone handling the bike.

config EBIKE_GEOFENCE_RADIUS_M
	int "Default geofence radius (metres)"
	default 500
	range 20 1000000
	help
	  Allowed radius around the home point. A value pushed through the
	  Device Shadow and persisted in NVS takes precedence.

# === Wheel speed sensor ======================================================

config EBIKE_WHEEL_CIRC_MM
	int "Default wheel circumference (millimetres)"
	default 2200
	range 500 4000
	help
	  Circumference of the wheel carrying the magnet (26" is about 2075 mm,
	  700C/28" 2100-2250 mm depending on the tyre). A value persisted in
	  NVS takes precedence.

config EBIKE_SPEED_DEBOUNCE_MS
	int "Speed sensor debounce (milliseconds)"
	default 20
	range 1 200
	help
	  Window during which edges following a pulse are ignored (reed bounce
	  is typically under 2 ms). It also bounds the maximum measurable
	  speed: 20 ms allows about 380 km/h with a 2.1 m wheel and one magnet.

config EBIKE_SPEED_STOP_TIMEOUT_S
	int "Wheel stopped timeout (seconds)"
	default 3
	range 1 30
	help
	  With no pulse for this long the speed drops to zero. 3 s means the
	  lowest detectable speed is around 2.5 km/h with a 2.1 m wheel.

# === GNSS ====================================================================

config EBIKE_GNSS_FIX_INTERVAL
	int "Interval between GNSS fixes (seconds, 1 = continuous)"
	default 1
	range 1 65535
	help
	  Passed to nrf_modem_gnss_fix_interval_set(). 1 means continuous
	  navigation (one PVT per second, instant re-fix in every free RF
	  window), which is what the batched sampling below expects. Values
	  between 2 and 9 are rejected by the modem.

config EBIKE_GNSS_FIX_RETRY
	int "Maximum duration of one fix attempt (seconds, 0 = unlimited)"
	default 0
	help
	  Time allowed to each periodic fix attempt. 0 lets the receiver search
	  without limit, which is what a cold start needs to download
	  ephemerides.

config EBIKE_TELEMETRY_SAMPLE_S
	int "Position sampling period (seconds)"
	default 5
	range 1 60
	help
	  Rate at which the last valid GNSS position is appended to the trace
	  buffer (only when a new fix arrived since the previous sample). The
	  buffer is drained and published as one grouped MQTT message per
	  supervision cycle.

config EBIKE_TELEMETRY_SAMPLE_PARKED_S
	int "Position sampling period while parked (seconds)"
	default 60
	range 1 3600
	help
	  Replaces EBIKE_TELEMETRY_SAMPLE_S in the PARKED state only; RIDING
	  and ALARM keep the fine rate.

	  A parked bike has not moved for EBIKE_PARK_TIMEOUT_S by construction,
	  so recording its position every 5 s produced 120 identical points per
	  cycle that then had to be flushed as eight consecutive MQTT messages.
	  The backlog catch-up, designed for outages, had become the permanent
	  regime of parking. At 60 s a parked cycle holds ten points and one
	  batch, with no functional loss: any movement switches back to RIDING
	  (or ALARM) and restores the fine rate immediately.

config EBIKE_TRACE_RING_SIZE
	int "Capacity of the GNSS trace buffer (samples)"
	default 240
	range 16 2048
	help
	  Position samples kept in RAM between two successful publications.
	  OFFLINE this is the depth of saved history: beyond it the oldest
	  points are overwritten and lost. Coverage = size x current sampling
	  rate, so 240 samples hold 20 min while riding and 4 h while parked.
	  Cost: 32 bytes per sample, 7.5 KB of RAM at the default size.

config EBIKE_GNSS_MAX_ACC_M
	int "Horizontal accuracy above which a fix is rejected (metres)"
	default 150
	range 20 10000
	help
	  Guard against clearly bad solutions: a fix less precise than this is
	  ignored entirely (no trace, no geofence, no last known fix).
	  Deliberately wide — the point is to reject garbage, not to filter on
	  quality. In continuous navigation, rejecting a fix costs nothing.

config EBIKE_GNSS_MAX_SPEED_KMH
	int "GNSS speed above which the fix speed is ignored (km/h)"
	default 60
	range 10 500
	help
	  The modem instantaneous Doppler speed is noisy at low speed and can
	  report several times the real value on an otherwise well located fix.
	  Above this threshold the speed is marked UNKNOWN (the `spd` field is
	  omitted from the point) while the POSITION is kept, since that is
	  what carries the trace.

config EBIKE_GNSS_MAX_SPEED_ACC_KMH
	int "Tolerated speed uncertainty (km/h, 0 = filter disabled)"
	default 0
	range 0 200
	help
	  Complementary statistical filter based on `speed_accuracy`, the
	  1-sigma figure the modem attaches to every PVT. DISABLED by default
	  on purpose: calibrating it blind risks discarding nearly every speed.
	  The status publishes the observed uncertainty (`sacc`, in 0.1 km/h)
	  so the threshold can be set from real data.

# === IMU =====================================================================

config EBIKE_IMU_POLL_MS
	int "Accelerometer polling period (milliseconds)"
	default 1000
	range 20 60000
	help
	  The lsm6ds0 driver has no trigger support, so the accelerometer is
	  polled. Do not go below the sensor ODR
	  (CONFIG_LSM6DS0_ACCEL_SAMPLING_RATE, 10 Hz by default, i.e. 100 ms).

module = EBIKE
module-str = eBike
source "${ZEPHYR_BASE}/subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
